flowchart LR

SRC["`What produces the signals`"]
  APP["`FastAPI API
N uvicorn workers`"]
SRC -.- APP
  WRK["`Celery worker`"]
  HOST["`The host machine`"]

M["`METRICS — 'THAT it is wrong'`"]
  MET["`/metrics
prometheus-fastapi-instrumentator
rate · latency · status per route`"]
M -.- MET
  OWN["`Exported BY THE APP — the 3 the HTTP
layer physically cannot see:
profplan_dependency_up (probe, 15s)
profplan_celery_queue_depth
profplan_llm_requests_total{provider,outcome}

DECISION: I export what something WATCHES,
not every number I could think of`"]
  NEX["`node-exporter
host CPU · memory · disk · network
'is the app slow' and 'is the box dying'
are two questions`"]
  FLW["`Flower
the individual task, its args, its traceback
Prometheus gives aggregates for alerts;
this answers WHICH one`"]
  PRM["`Prometheus :9090
scrapes /metrics, NOT /ready —
readiness is for the orchestrator,
metrics is for monitoring`"]
  MET --> PRM
  OWN --> PRM
  NEX --> PRM
  FLW --> PRM

L["`LOGS — 'WHAT the user did'`"]
  STD["`single-line JSON to stdout
no files, no rotation —
a container should not know Loki exists`"]
L -.- STD
  RLM["`RequestLoggingMiddleware — ONE line per request
method · route · status · latency · IP · UA
acting user (id, email, role) · trace_id
one line, not three: half a story across
two lines is unqueryable

GOTCHA FIXED: this serialization was on the
event loop and cost real throughput —
moved off it in its own commit`"]
  PTL["`Promtail
discovers containers via the Docker socket
→ a new service is collected with zero config`"]
  LOK["`Loki :3100`"]
  STD --> RLM --> PTL --> LOK

T["`TRACES — 'WHERE the time went'`"]
  OTL["`OpenTelemetry, opt-in (OTEL_ENABLED)
auto-instruments FastAPI · SQLAlchemy ·
Redis · httpx · Celery`"]
T -.- OTL
  PROP["`context PROPAGATES THROUGH THE REDIS BROKER
→ the HTTP request and the background job
that outlived it are ONE trace`"]
  OTC["`OTel Collector :4317/:4318
my code talks OTLP to this, never to Tempo —
changing backend is one container's config,
not a change across 13 modules`"]
  TMP["`Tempo
no UI of its own · not published to the host
Grafana is the only window`"]
  OTL --> PROP --> OTC --> TMP

GRF["`Grafana :3000
3 datasources, all PROVISIONED AS CODE
dashboard JSON lives in the repo
a dashboard that exists only in one browser
is a personal note, not infrastructure`"]

PRM --> GRF
LOK --> GRF
TMP --> GRF

LINK["`THE LINK IS THE PRODUCT

log line → trace_id → TraceQL → the span
{container=...} | json | user_email=...

MEASURED ON A LIVE STACK:
POST /documents 118ms → returns 202
worker run/documents.ingest 4586ms
POST (embedding) 4351ms
30 spans · 2 processes · 1 trace

→ 93% of ingestion was the EMBEDDING CALL
no aggregate metric would say that
without it I'd have optimized the parser
and made 7% of the problem faster`"]

GRF ==> LINK

A["`ALERTING — a metric nobody looks at is not monitoring`"]
  RUL["`12 rules, versioned in the repo
ApiDown · HighServerErrorRate (>2% 5xx/5m)
LatencyP95Degraded (>1s/10m — baseline 545ms MEASURED)
DependencyDown · CeleryQueueBacklog/Stalled
CeleryTaskFailures · LlmAllProvidersFailing
LlmProviderCircuitOpen · HostDisk/Memory`"]
A -.- RUL
  WD["`Watchdog — fires ALWAYS, on purpose
an alert that never fired is indistinguishable
from a broken one · its SILENCE is the signal`"]
  ALM["`Alertmanager :9093
groups · INHIBITS symptoms of a cause
it already reported · routes`"]
  RB["`every rule carries a runbook annotation
→ docs/observability/ALERTS.md
an alert without a runbook is a 3am scare`"]
  CI["`CI VALIDATES ALL OF IT
promtool check rules · amtool check-config
· dashboard JSON
WHY: a broken rule file makes Prometheus start
with NO ALERTS AT ALL and tell nobody —
a silent failure in the anti-silence system`"]
  RUL --- WD
  RUL --> ALM
  RUL --- RB
  RUL --- CI

PRM ==> RUL
PANEL["`EVERY PANEL BACKS A RULE
if it pages nobody it is decoration,
and decoration trains your eye to skip the screen`"]
GRF --- PANEL

APP --> MET
APP --> STD
APP --> OTL
WRK --> STD
WRK --> OTL
WRK --> FLW
HOST --> NEX

